====================================================
Domain Context – Bromatología Inspection System
====================================================

This project is an internal inspection management system used by a municipal food safety authority (Bromatología).

The backend is implemented with:
- Flask
- SQLAlchemy ORM
- Alembic migrations
- Modular architecture under app/domains

The frontend is implemented with React + MUI.

The system manages inspections, notifications, violations, administrative procedures, and inspection routes.

Important: existing modules and endpoints must not be broken unless explicitly instructed.

----------------------------------------------------

Core Concept of the New Architecture

The system is evolving from a model centered on "actuaciones" (inspection records) to a model centered on:

1. Work triggers (iniciadores)
2. Work planning (inspection routes)
3. Work execution (completing tasks)
4. Administrative follow-up (expedientes and oficios)

----------------------------------------------------

Work Triggers (Iniciadores)

A work trigger represents a reason for an inspection visit.

Possible triggers include:

- relevamiento (field survey)
- denuncia (complaint)
- reinspeccion after notification expiration
- verificar e informar (from oficio)
- ratificacion de clausura (from oficio)
- ratificacion de decomiso (from oficio)

All triggers must be normalized into a unified operational entity called:

iniciador_ruta

This entity feeds the route planning system.

----------------------------------------------------

Route Planning

Inspection routes organize work assignments.

New entities required:

ruta_trabajo
    represents an inspection route for a given date and shift

ruta_grupo
    represents a group of inspectors assigned to a route

ruta_grupo_inspector
    relation between inspectors and groups

ruta_item
    represents a single work task within a route

A ruta_item references an iniciador_ruta and contains execution state.

----------------------------------------------------

Work Execution

Inspectors complete assigned tasks through the "complete work" flow.

A completed task may generate one or more inspection documents:

- acta de inspeccion
- acta de notificacion
- acta de comprobacion
- acta de clausura
- acta de decomiso

Rules:

If both NOTIFICACION and COMPROBACION are produced in the same visit,
both must be saved but the dominant future flow is COMPROBACION.

----------------------------------------------------

Administrative Flow

Administrative procedures include:

expediente
oficio

Rules:

- An oficio always belongs to an expediente.
- A comprobacion may generate an expediente for sending the case.
- Later, an oficio response may arrive with a different expediente.
- Therefore multiple expedientes may exist in the lifecycle of the same case.

----------------------------------------------------

Not Executed Work

When completing a task, it may not be executed.

Possible reasons:

LOCAL_CERRADO
INCLEMENCIA_TIEMPO
NO_EXISTE_LOCAL
OTRO

Rules:

LOCAL_CERRADO
    task returns to pending queue

INCLEMENCIA_TIEMPO
    task returns to pending queue

OTRO
    task normally returns to pending queue

NO_EXISTE_LOCAL
    the origin trigger must be logically closed so it will not be scheduled again

Never physically delete records for this case. Use logical closure.

